NAME
       localectl - show or set the system language and keyboard layout

SYNOPSIS
       localectl [status]
       localectl list-locales
       localectl set-locale LANG=LOCALE
       localectl set-keymap MAP

DESCRIPTION
       localectl shows the system-wide locale (language, number and date
       formats) and the keyboard layout for the text console and for
       graphical sessions. The settings are stored in /etc/locale.conf and
       /etc/vconsole.conf and apply to new logins.

COMMANDS
       status
              Show the current settings (the default).

       list-locales
              List the locales that are installed. More come with the
              glibc-langpack-* packages.

       set-locale LANG=LOCALE
              Set the system locale, for example LANG=en_US.UTF-8.

       set-keymap MAP
              Set the console keyboard layout, for example us or de.

EXAMPLES
           localectl
           localectl list-locales

FILES
       /etc/locale.conf, /etc/vconsole.conf

SEE ALSO
       timedatectl(1), hostnamectl(1), locale(1)
